WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:15.000
Introduction. Words have different jobs in a sentence. Learn eight common parts of speech.
Read each definition and example.

2
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Nouns. A noun names a person, place, thing, or idea.
The teacher opened the book.

3
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:45.000
Pronouns. A pronoun takes the place of a noun or noun phrase.
Amina is reading. She likes stories.

4
00:00:45.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Verbs. A verb expresses an action or a state.
The children play. The room is quiet.

5
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:15.000
Adjectives. An adjective describes a noun or pronoun.
The small bird has blue feathers.

6
00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:30.000
Adverbs. An adverb can describe a verb, adjective, or another adverb.
She reads carefully. It is very cold.

7
00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:45.000
Prepositions. A preposition shows a relationship, often of place or time.
The bag is under the table.

8
00:01:45.000 --> 00:02:00.000
Conjunctions. A conjunction joins words, phrases, or clauses.
I wanted to play, but it rained.

9
00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:15.000
Interjections. An interjection expresses a sudden feeling or reaction.
Wow! That is a beautiful painting.

10
00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:30.000
Summary & Practice. A word can have different jobs in different sentences. Look at how it is used.
I drink water. / I need a drink.
